1
00:01:04,340 --> 00:01:07,660
=Bionic Trace=

2
00:01:07,740 --> 00:01:10,620
=Episode 15=

3
00:01:10,660 --> 00:01:11,230
(Acclaimed novelist's
thrilling mystery masterpiece)

4
00:01:11,230 --> 00:01:12,590
(The Survivor book signing)
(Zhang Mingxuan?)

5
00:01:12,910 --> 00:01:14,080
(But his previous works)

6
00:01:14,080 --> 00:01:15,800
(were all mediocre novels.)

7
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:17,270
(Then he suddenly wrote)

8
00:01:17,270 --> 00:01:19,190
(such a brilliant mystery novel.)

9
00:01:20,590 --> 00:01:21,440
(There's more to him
than meets the eye.)

10
00:01:21,760 --> 00:01:22,230
(Ada.)

11
00:01:22,360 --> 00:01:23,310
(Go check him out.)

12
00:01:26,800 --> 00:01:27,760
Song Yang.

13
00:01:27,950 --> 00:01:28,720
I think the first step

14
00:01:28,720 --> 00:01:30,080
should be to test him.

15
00:01:30,400 --> 00:01:31,440
(Do you have any ideas?)

16
00:01:32,190 --> 00:01:33,830
You're finally thinking before acting.

17
00:01:34,080 --> 00:01:35,760
Start with his writing techniques.

18
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:37,400
You might find something suspicious.

19
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:38,630
Understood.

20
00:01:49,870 --> 00:01:50,550
Mr. Zhang.

21
00:01:50,630 --> 00:01:51,870
I'm a fan of your books.

22
00:01:52,400 --> 00:01:53,040
Hello.

23
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:55,440
Would you like a personal message?

24
00:01:55,630 --> 00:01:56,440
Mr. Zhang.

25
00:01:56,680 --> 00:01:58,550
In Chapter Six of your book,

26
00:01:58,680 --> 00:02:00,190
you described the killer
strangling the victim,

27
00:02:00,400 --> 00:02:02,120
the victim's tongue slowly protruding,

28
00:02:02,190 --> 00:02:03,870
eyes bloodshot,

29
00:02:04,270 --> 00:02:06,000
feet gripping the edge of the bed.

30
00:02:06,590 --> 00:02:09,000
That instinctive struggle before death

31
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:10,190
felt incredibly realistic.

32
00:02:10,600 --> 00:02:11,190
Could you tell me

33
00:02:11,190 --> 00:02:12,600
how you came up with it?

34
00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:13,830
I just

35
00:02:13,830 --> 00:02:15,110
consulted some reference materials.

36
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:17,550
And in the second half of the novel,

37
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:20,190
the killer strangles the victim

38
00:02:20,240 --> 00:02:22,000
and plunges a knife into his eye socket.

39
00:02:22,270 --> 00:02:23,030
With a thud,

40
00:02:24,160 --> 00:02:25,390
the man, already dead,

41
00:02:25,390 --> 00:02:26,750
continues to twitch.

42
00:02:30,540 --> 00:02:33,340
(The Survivor, Zhang Mingxuan)

43
00:02:42,830 --> 00:02:45,000
I can hardly imagine such a scene.

44
00:02:45,830 --> 00:02:46,830
I'd like to know where

45
00:02:46,830 --> 00:02:48,110
you got your inspiration.

46
00:02:48,800 --> 00:02:49,830
Could you tell me?

47
00:02:52,630 --> 00:02:53,670
Young lady.

48
00:02:55,360 --> 00:02:57,600
You seem to have a lot of questions.

49
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:00,190
Who are you?

50
00:03:06,440 --> 00:03:07,550
I'm sorry.

51
00:03:07,550 --> 00:03:09,000
I think I need a break.

52
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:11,360
Sorry.

53
00:03:12,750 --> 00:03:13,800
There's definitely something
suspicious about him.

54
00:03:14,030 --> 00:03:15,390
I suspect he has

55
00:03:15,390 --> 00:03:16,720
a more direct connection to the killer.

56
00:03:17,390 --> 00:03:18,630
I'll keep following him.

57
00:04:09,110 --> 00:04:10,470
(Mingxuan.)

58
00:04:10,470 --> 00:04:11,880
(Are you coming over today?)

59
00:04:15,670 --> 00:04:16,760
I'll be there soon.

60
00:04:35,020 --> 00:04:37,100
(Liu Siqi, Ophthalmology,
Bed 20, Wishing You a Speedy Recovery)

61
00:04:44,880 --> 00:04:45,690
Siqi.

62
00:04:47,760 --> 00:04:49,670
I've downloaded some new novels for you.

63
00:04:49,790 --> 00:04:51,000
You can listen to them

64
00:04:51,160 --> 00:04:52,160
when you're bored.

65
00:04:52,230 --> 00:04:53,950
Thank you, Mingxuan.

66
00:04:54,760 --> 00:04:55,790
Are any of them

67
00:04:56,040 --> 00:04:57,040
your books?

68
00:04:58,760 --> 00:05:00,160
My writing isn't very good.

69
00:05:00,640 --> 00:05:01,160
Well,

70
00:05:01,200 --> 00:05:03,000
I'll show you someday.

71
00:05:04,600 --> 00:05:05,830
I mean,

72
00:05:06,790 --> 00:05:08,230
I can read them to you.

73
00:05:08,390 --> 00:05:09,200
Mingxuan.

74
00:05:10,390 --> 00:05:12,600
Thank you for visiting me every week.

75
00:05:13,150 --> 00:05:14,090
If only

76
00:05:14,760 --> 00:05:16,270
I knew what you

77
00:05:16,270 --> 00:05:17,230
looked like.

78
00:05:24,830 --> 00:05:26,480
Use your hands as your eyes.

79
00:05:32,880 --> 00:05:34,350
So you're this young.

80
00:05:34,350 --> 00:05:35,860
I always felt

81
00:05:36,640 --> 00:05:37,950
you were a lot like my dad.

82
00:05:40,390 --> 00:05:41,830
Do I seem that old?

83
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:50,070
Mingxuan.

84
00:05:50,270 --> 00:05:51,510
I'm a little thirsty.

85
00:05:51,600 --> 00:05:53,270
Could you get me some water?

86
00:05:54,880 --> 00:05:55,640
Sure.

87
00:06:09,550 --> 00:06:11,000
That's a brain-computer interface.

88
00:06:13,640 --> 00:06:14,790
An interface?

89
00:06:21,440 --> 00:06:22,000
Here.

90
00:06:22,040 --> 00:06:22,670
Siqi.

91
00:06:22,760 --> 00:06:23,720
Here's your water.

92
00:06:24,320 --> 00:06:24,760
Here.

93
00:06:24,830 --> 00:06:25,600
Careful.

94
00:06:33,270 --> 00:06:34,380
This girl

95
00:06:35,200 --> 00:06:36,830
seems to be Zhang Mingxuan's

96
00:06:36,950 --> 00:06:37,760
younger sister.

97
00:06:39,720 --> 00:06:41,160
But their interactions

98
00:06:41,160 --> 00:06:42,320
aren't typical of siblings.

99
00:06:42,790 --> 00:06:44,320
Brain-computer interfaces in humans

100
00:06:44,320 --> 00:06:45,790
are strictly regulated.

101
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:47,440
Under normal circumstances,

102
00:06:47,440 --> 00:06:49,390
citizens aren't allowed to install them
without authorization.

103
00:06:51,790 --> 00:06:53,200
Perhaps there's someone

104
00:06:54,200 --> 00:06:55,790
who knows where Zhang Mingxuan

105
00:06:55,790 --> 00:06:56,830
got his brain-computer interface.

106
00:07:06,510 --> 00:07:07,040
Hello?

107
00:07:07,790 --> 00:07:08,530
Zhou Zicheng.

108
00:07:09,040 --> 00:07:10,000
Sorry, it's not convenient for me

109
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:11,440
to meet you in person.

110
00:07:11,790 --> 00:07:13,000
How have you been lately?

111
00:07:13,320 --> 00:07:14,200
(I'm doing fine.)

112
00:07:14,760 --> 00:07:15,760
(The police want to use me)

113
00:07:15,760 --> 00:07:17,480
(to lure out
other black-market operations.)

114
00:07:18,200 --> 00:07:19,670
So they've kept me here.

115
00:07:21,160 --> 00:07:22,160
I have no choice but to stay.

116
00:07:23,350 --> 00:07:24,390
But look at you.

117
00:07:24,640 --> 00:07:25,600
I haven't seen you in a few days.

118
00:07:25,760 --> 00:07:26,350
How did you

119
00:07:26,640 --> 00:07:27,790
(end up becoming a wanted fugitive?)

120
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:28,670
Yes.

121
00:07:29,110 --> 00:07:30,440
That's why I'm contacting you

122
00:07:30,440 --> 00:07:32,350
through an encrypted connection.

123
00:07:32,830 --> 00:07:33,950
I don't have much time.

124
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:35,000
(If you want to know why)

125
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:36,000
(I'm wanted by the police...)

126
00:07:36,200 --> 00:07:37,000
It's okay.

127
00:07:37,200 --> 00:07:38,230
No need to explain.

128
00:07:38,790 --> 00:07:40,000
Just get to the point.

129
00:07:40,160 --> 00:07:41,390
Consider it repayment for your help.

130
00:07:41,670 --> 00:07:42,510
Thank you.

131
00:07:42,790 --> 00:07:44,000
I'm contacting you this time

132
00:07:44,160 --> 00:07:45,200
because I need your advice

133
00:07:45,200 --> 00:07:46,640
about brain-computer interfaces.

134
00:07:47,270 --> 00:07:48,270
Does the black market

135
00:07:48,390 --> 00:07:50,000
offer illegal brain-computer interface

136
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:51,670
(implantation services for humans?)

137
00:07:55,600 --> 00:07:56,920
Yes.

138
00:07:56,920 --> 00:07:58,070
It does.

139
00:07:59,480 --> 00:08:01,200
I've performed a few myself.

140
00:08:01,880 --> 00:08:03,760
But I've already told the police
about all that.

141
00:08:04,110 --> 00:08:05,720
Do you know Zhang Mingxuan?

142
00:08:06,950 --> 00:08:07,720
(Ada.)

143
00:08:08,230 --> 00:08:09,440
(People who come to us)

144
00:08:09,440 --> 00:08:10,670
(never use their real names.)

145
00:08:10,790 --> 00:08:12,270
He's a novelist.

146
00:08:12,420 --> 00:08:13,440
(Hold, End call)

147
00:08:13,440 --> 00:08:15,830
(I think I remember someone like that.)

148
00:08:16,390 --> 00:08:18,790
(He said he was lacking inspiration.)

149
00:08:19,200 --> 00:08:20,070
(Besides getting)

150
00:08:20,070 --> 00:08:21,390
(a brain-computer interface,)

151
00:08:21,390 --> 00:08:23,070
(he also bought some memory cards.)

152
00:08:24,000 --> 00:08:25,200
Memory cards?

153
00:08:25,600 --> 00:08:26,390
Oh, right.

154
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:31,390
I'm not proud of this,

155
00:08:31,920 --> 00:08:33,350
(but to avoid potential)

156
00:08:33,350 --> 00:08:34,470
(disputes with customers,)

157
00:08:34,790 --> 00:08:37,000
(we secretly back up their memories)

158
00:08:37,590 --> 00:08:38,960
(as leverage.)

159
00:08:39,520 --> 00:08:41,400
(We also erase names and locations)

160
00:08:41,400 --> 00:08:42,840
and other sensitive information

161
00:08:42,910 --> 00:08:43,590
before selling the memories

162
00:08:43,590 --> 00:08:44,760
to people who need them,

163
00:08:44,760 --> 00:08:45,590
like novelists.

164
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:46,790
Have you ever seen

165
00:08:46,790 --> 00:08:48,470
the memories sold to Zhang Mingxuan?

166
00:08:49,110 --> 00:08:49,960
(No, I haven't.)

167
00:08:50,320 --> 00:08:51,520
The processing of backed-up memories

168
00:08:51,520 --> 00:08:52,790
is all handled by AI.

169
00:08:53,350 --> 00:08:54,110
You know,

170
00:08:54,280 --> 00:08:55,280
in our line of work,

171
00:08:55,280 --> 00:08:56,350
the more you know,

172
00:08:56,670 --> 00:08:57,590
the more danger you're in.

173
00:08:57,590 --> 00:08:59,400
The encrypted connection
only lasts 30 seconds.

174
00:08:59,590 --> 00:09:00,760
One last question.

175
00:09:01,080 --> 00:09:03,790
Could connecting a memory card directly
through a brain-computer interface

176
00:09:04,080 --> 00:09:05,590
cause personality changes

177
00:09:05,590 --> 00:09:06,590
in the user?

178
00:09:06,710 --> 00:09:07,470
What?

179
00:09:08,470 --> 00:09:09,230
No, I...

180
00:09:09,840 --> 00:09:11,080
I explicitly told him

181
00:09:11,080 --> 00:09:12,520
to use an external device to view them.

182
00:09:12,520 --> 00:09:13,760
Connecting directly through
a brain-computer interface

183
00:09:13,880 --> 00:09:15,400
is an extremely foolish thing to do.

184
00:09:15,640 --> 00:09:17,000
At best, it could cause hallucinations.

185
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:17,790
At worst,

186
00:09:18,030 --> 00:09:19,000
the person could

187
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:20,150
become someone else entirely!

188
00:09:22,230 --> 00:09:24,110
So Zhang Mingxuan

189
00:09:24,350 --> 00:09:25,710
has been taken over
by another personality?

190
00:09:26,230 --> 00:09:27,280
More precisely,

191
00:09:27,880 --> 00:09:29,880
the murderer's memories
on the memory card

192
00:09:30,200 --> 00:09:32,080
have overwritten part
of Zhang Mingxuan's personality.

193
00:09:32,320 --> 00:09:34,640
So if we get that memory card,

194
00:09:34,960 --> 00:09:35,910
we can find out

195
00:09:35,910 --> 00:09:37,350
what connection this serial killer

196
00:09:37,350 --> 00:09:38,790
has to Cedar.

197
00:09:40,790 --> 00:09:41,840
I'll go right now.

198
00:10:05,460 --> 00:10:10,860
(Zhang Mingxuan)

199
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:18,910
I'm inside.

200
00:10:19,400 --> 00:10:20,200
(I've already hacked into)

201
00:10:20,200 --> 00:10:21,670
(Zhang Mingxuan's home network.)

202
00:10:21,670 --> 00:10:23,110
(He doesn't have any
surveillance cameras.)

203
00:10:23,280 --> 00:10:23,840
(Ada.)

204
00:10:23,960 --> 00:10:25,710
(I need you to share
your vision with me.)

205
00:10:32,580 --> 00:10:34,940
(Silence)

206
00:10:34,960 --> 00:10:35,590
(God,)

207
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:37,550
(Zhang Mingxuan, book sales report)
(what a messy shut-in.)

208
00:10:37,760 --> 00:10:38,960
(From the looks of it, the memory card)

209
00:10:38,960 --> 00:10:40,200
(could be anywhere.)

210
00:10:40,520 --> 00:10:42,400
(But judging by his appliance usage,)

211
00:10:42,640 --> 00:10:44,320
(Zhang Mingxuan has gone to sleep.)

212
00:10:44,320 --> 00:10:45,640
(As long as you're quiet,)

213
00:10:45,640 --> 00:10:46,590
(there shouldn't be a problem.)

214
00:10:47,910 --> 00:10:48,760
Okay.

215
00:10:49,150 --> 00:10:51,080
Scanning electromagnetic signals.

216
00:10:57,110 --> 00:10:58,710
It seems to be in this bookcase.

217
00:11:02,860 --> 00:11:03,710
Got it.

218
00:11:06,110 --> 00:11:07,400
Like what you see?

219
00:11:08,640 --> 00:11:09,640
Android.

220
00:11:20,920 --> 00:11:28,200
♪I'm the one who's broken♪

221
00:11:29,030 --> 00:11:33,900
♪Calm, ordinary, and reckless♪

222
00:11:33,940 --> 00:11:36,810
♪That's me, too♪

223
00:11:38,350 --> 00:11:41,870
♪Carefully sketching
and shaping every detail♪

224
00:11:42,700 --> 00:11:46,170
♪Laughter and tears make life feel real♪

225
00:11:46,790 --> 00:11:50,580
♪Don't fear that it's not worth it.
Just be brave♪

226
00:11:50,900 --> 00:11:53,430
♪And learn from your mistakes♪

227
00:11:55,370 --> 00:11:58,030
♪If the human heart
is impossible to fathom♪

228
00:11:58,030 --> 00:12:00,160
♪Could selling my soul and body♪

229
00:12:00,160 --> 00:12:03,330
♪Bring me something more?♪

230
00:12:04,030 --> 00:12:10,760
♪Stroke by stroke,
I draw the perfect outline♪

231
00:12:11,590 --> 00:12:14,990
♪Sadness is blue♪

232
00:12:15,970 --> 00:12:19,210
♪How would you paint me?♪

233
00:12:20,210 --> 00:12:23,940
♪Layering, crossing, blending endlessly♪

234
00:12:24,040 --> 00:12:26,200
♪Painting without restraint♪

235
00:12:26,390 --> 00:12:28,980
♪Covering the person I used to be♪

236
00:12:28,980 --> 00:12:33,170
♪If I could start over♪

237
00:12:33,340 --> 00:12:37,240
♪I'd show more feeling
in every look and gesture♪

238
00:12:37,350 --> 00:12:39,990
♪Give me back my smile♪

239
00:12:40,590 --> 00:12:43,070
♪Find joy even in hardship♪

240
00:12:43,570 --> 00:12:48,810
♪Don't let the next version of me
be left with nothing♪
